WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.020
Hey everyone, welcome to Tesla Short's time, Daily Episode 524 for June 27th, 2026.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.020
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver. Let's dive into today's Tesla news.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:20.100
NHTSA ending its power steering probe on 376,000 Teslas clears one regulatory overhang for the company.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:26.260
The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration closed its investigation into power steering

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:33.060
loss reports affecting certain Tesla models. The probe had examined roughly 376,000 vehicles,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.560
closure removes an active regulatory review that had been open on the issue.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:43.640
Listeners should watch whether similar investigations surface on other vehicle systems in coming quarters.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:50.060
This regulatory relief now opens the door to forward-looking analyst views on growth programs.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:57.460
Elizabeth Pramila moved her rating from buy to strong buy after previously holding a bearish stance.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:04.280
She points to CyberCab production starting with the unboxed process and a 2 million unit annual target.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:11.340
Optimus scaling toward 2027 with suppliers already secured also factored into the upgrade.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.520
The analyst treats both programs as medium-term revenue drivers rather than distance speculation.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.580
Yesterday, the show covered the latest CyberCab and Optimus regulatory and production updates.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:28.640
This upgrade adds investor sentiment data that builds directly on those timelines.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:35.220
The next data point to watch is any supplier confirmation or production line video from Giga, Texas.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:40.620
Wall Street consensus now sits at 406,000 deliveries for the second quarter.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.300
The figure reflects modest sequential growth from Q1.

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:51.080
Analysts are modeling continued energy storage contribution to offset any vehicle margin pressure.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:55.960
The number will be compared against actual results when Tesla reports in July.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:02:03.040
Morgan Stanley separately lifted its own Q2 delivery estimate while keeping its price target unchanged.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:08.720
The adjustment reflects stronger than expected order momentum in Europe and North America.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:15.360
That sets up the next thread around factory level expansion plans. Tesla filed plans for an

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.740
additional production building and dedicated rail terminal at the Brandenburg site.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:25.600
The rail connection would support higher inbound component volumes and outbound vehicle shipments.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:30.900
The expansion sits alongside earlier hiring increases at the same factory.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:36.920
Observers will watch construction permits and any announced timeline for the new infrastructure.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:42.440
The company also announced plans to add another 1,000 positions at Giga Berlin.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:48.520
The move follows rising European EV registrations and internal production targets.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:53.120
Hiring focuses on assembly and logistics roles tied to the new building.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:59.540
The increase keeps the site on a growth trajectory even as some legacy automakers announced cuts elsewhere.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:07.160
Volkswagen outlined plans to reduce its workforce by up to 100,000 positions over several years.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:13.340
The cuts respond to slower EV adoption in its traditional markets and rising competition from

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:19.780
Chinese brands. Tesla's lower cost production methods and Chinese manufacturers pricing pressure

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:25.740
are cited as contributing factors. The scale of the reduction highlights the cost gap legacy

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:32.800
platforms still face. Federal regulators ease certain operational rules for autonomous ride hailing

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:38.460
services. The change reduces the number of safety drivers required during testing in select

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:45.700
jurisdictions. Tesla, Amazon, ZUX and Waymo stand to benefit from lower per mile operating costs

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:52.160
during early deployment. The next milestone is state level adoption of the revised Federal baseline.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:58.100
European buyers can now configure the signature edition model as through the configurator without

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:03.420
prior announcement. The variant carries updated interior and exterior details.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:09.960
Availability signals continued support for the refreshed sedan line even as focus remains on higher

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:16.180
volume models. European order data and coming weeks will show whether the edition moves volume.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:21.680
The configurator listing appeared on the same day as other European market updates.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.980
No separate press release accompanied the edition of the signature edition.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:32.840
The move keeps the model S available alongside higher volume refreshed vehicles. Tesla deployed

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:38.440
its 1,000th supercharging stall in Australia with the commissioning of a new stall in the country.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:44.240
Australia now joins a small group of markets with over 1,000 Tesla superchargers.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:51.160
The addition supports longer distance travel corridors and growing model Y and model 3 registrations.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:55.260
Future expansion will focus on regional routes still lacking coverage.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:00.800
The milestone stall was added to an existing site rather than a brand new location.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.920
Network growth in Australia has tracked rising local registrations of Tesla vehicles.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:11.660
Tesla filed for the Megapod trademark covering a self-contained AI compute unit.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:18.400
The system would repurpose idle supercharger stalls as edge data centers when vehicles are not charging.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:23.300
The approach leverages existing power infrastructure and real estate footprint.

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:29.240
Commercial deployment would depend on Dojo software optimizations and utility agreements.

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:33.540
The trademark filing lists the unit as a modular hardware package.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:38.520
No timeline for pilot installations has been released alongside the application.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:44.780
A recently published patent describes a new thermal pump architecture but does not state it is

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:50.580
already in production vehicles. Confirmation would require tear down reports or official Tesla

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:57.020
documentation. The filing shows Tesla continues to refine cooling systems even after the Highland

00:05:57.020 --> 00:06:02.860
and Juniper refreshes. Observers will look for any service part updates that matched the patent

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:08.640
to design. The application was published without diagrams indicating current hardware fitment.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:13.380
No reference appears to specific model years or production dates in the text.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:19.200
An owner shared video of descending steep grades in Pennsylvania where tractor trailers must

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:25.240
use mandatory pull-off areas. The footage highlights how regenerative braking and one pedal driving

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:31.640
handle sustained downhill loads differently than traditional trucks. Other drivers in the replies

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:37.720
compare notes on similar routes in the Rockies and Alps. The clip underscores real world conditions

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:42.160
where EV torque and braking behavior stand out from ICE vehicles.

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:48.700
Comments noted the absence of brake fade during the long descent. Several viewers asked for battery

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:54.520
percentage data at the bottom of the grade. Testorati reminded owners that preconditioning at home

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:59.880
overnight remains the most efficient way to start a long trip. The advice centers on using the

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:05.100
vehicle's scheduled departure feature so the battery reaches optimal temperature without drawing

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:10.780
from superchargers and route. Owners and northern climates noted the tip also helps with cabin

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:17.520
preconditioning in winter. The post reflects ongoing community focus on minimizing paid charging stops.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:23.260
Scheduled departure can be set the night before departure through the Tesla app. Users reported

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:29.780
lower total energy cost when following the preconditioning sequence. An 84-year-old driver completed

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:36.060
the trip to the Arctic Ocean in a Tesla documenting the journey on social media. The route required

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:41.920
careful planning around charging availability in remote northern Canada. The story has circulated

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:48.360
among owners interested in extreme range travel. It adds another data point to real world cold weather

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:54.160
and long distance capability discussions. The driver posted photos at the final coastal point

00:07:54.160 --> 00:08:00.360
after several days of travel. Charging stops were spaced to account for reduced range in sub-zero

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:06.780
temperatures. Photos of the refreshed model Y interior surface showing updated materials and layout

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:12.780
changes. The images reveal revised center console and door panel designs compared with current

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:18.920
production cars. Owners are debating whether the changes improve perceived quality or simply refresh

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:25.360
styling. The leak gives an early look at what buyers may see when the updated vehicle reaches showrooms.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:32.200
The console appears lower and wider than the current version. Door panel show new stitching patterns

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:38.120
and material textures. The company reached a confidential settlement in the case involving a model Y

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:44.920
using FSD that struck a pedestrian. Details of the agreement remain private. Leaving open questions

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:50.740
about how Tesla will adjust future safety communications. The resolution avoids a public trial but

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:56.480
does not alter the broader regulatory scrutiny surrounding driver assistance claims. The settlement

00:08:56.480 --> 00:09:02.380
was filed in a California court earlier this week. No admission of liability was included in the

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:08.440
public docket. Vehicle ownership costs over a decade and a half are shaped more by energy price

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:14.600
volatility and maintenance schedules than by the sticker price paid on day one. A direct comparison

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:19.660
between a Tesla and a comparable Toyota gas model shows the electric car pulling ahead once

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:25.700
electricity rates and fewer service visits are factored in. The gap narrows if home charging is

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:32.140
unavailable and public rates stay high. The real variable is not the battery itself but whether owners

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:38.920
can lock in low cost overnight power for most of their miles. That same long-term math changes again

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:44.860
when Robo Taxes enter the picture. If a personal vehicle sits idle 95% of the time,

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:50.580
the capital tied up in its battery and body becomes an expensive asset with low utilization.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:56.960
Shifting those miles onto a shared fleet spreads the same hardware cost across many more trips per day.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:02.900
The industry precedent that matters here is not another car company but the smartphone transition

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:08.640
from ownership to shared data plans. Early buyers paid full price for handsets while later users

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:14.020
accepted lower hardware margins in exchange for service contracts that guaranteed recurring revenue.

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:20.160
Tesla's energy and autonomy businesses sit at a similar inflection where the hardware still needs

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:25.720
to be built. The margin may increasingly come from the miles or electrons that flow through it

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:31.340
rather than from the initial transaction. Keep an eye on supplier updates tied to the optimist

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:36.220
and cybercab timelines discussed today. That covers it for today's Tesla developments.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:48.740
TSLA closed at $379.71, up $5.31, 1.4%. Share this episode with a fellow Tesla enthusiast

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:54.640
if you found it useful and subscribe so you don't miss tomorrow's episode. I'm Patrick and Vancouver

